From b24888f6a7aa20d5328481dc1af09bf5e09855db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sonnet <noreply@example.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 13:05:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ci): stop flaky 5s test timeouts, make CI failures
 diagnosable

First GitHub Actions run failed in the "Tests (zero-skip gate)" step with
"1 test/file failed" while the database preflight had succeeded. The message
"KB_TEST_DATABASE_URL or DATABASE_URL is required" quoted from that run is the
*expected* output of the green negative-control step, not the failure cause,
but it was emitted as a red ::error:: annotation and hid the real problem.

- vitest.config.ts: testTimeout/hookTimeout 60s (default 5s is too tight for
  three heavy tests on a shared runner: jalali 1200-1600 sweep, 25 random
  seeds, 12-round verify/correct race). Explicit per-test timeouts untouched.
  retry stays off on purpose (would hide real flakiness).
- tooling/ci-tests.ts: describeFailures() prints failing test name + first
  error line to log, annotations and step summary; gateAnnotation() downgrades
  the negative-control ::error:: to a labelled ::notice::.
- .github/workflows/ci.yml: negative-control step sets CI_GATE_SELF_CHECK=1.
- tooling/ci-diagnostics.test.ts (12) and tooling/vitest-config.test.ts (4):
  new tests for the new behaviour (631 passed, 0 skipped, 0 failed, 16 todo).
- docs: ADR-0007, handoff 0009, known-pitfalls.

No existing test and no file under src/ was modified.
